    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d466">

                <pb facs="0763" n="737" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v16/pg737"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">751G.00/5–954: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The United States Delegation to the Department of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top
                            secret<lb/>niact</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-05-09T12:00:00+01:00">May 9, 1954—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Dulte 56. Personal for Secretary. Reference your Tedul 42.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d466-f1"/> I put the point covered in the reference paragraph of
                    your speech to the French in a broad and unmistakable hint in my private talk
                    with Bidault last Friday.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d466-f2"/> He got the point and
                    it had, I think, a great deal to do with stiffening his position.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
